From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 05:14:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(system): list the options each loaded model was given

LocalAI completes a model's config before it loads it: the context size
and GPU layers guessed from the GGUF, the hardware auto-tuning, the
application's runtime settings. What the backend actually received is
therefore in no file and on no endpoint, only in a DEBUG log line. A
client that must know exactly how a model runs, to tell two runs apart
or to notice that a reload changed them, cannot read it.

Record the options sent with LoadModel on the loaded model, and list
them in GET /system's loaded_models together with their
EffectiveModelOptionsHash, the hash the distributed registry already
keeps per replica:

  "load_options": {"Model": "bge-m3.gguf", "ContextSize": 8192, ...},
  "load_options_hash": "6f1c..."

Single node only: a model a remote worker holds lists none. /system is
an admin route. The options carry no key (the proxy options name a
key's variable or file, not the key), but a model's `env:` is copied
into them, as the DEBUG log already shows.

The swagger entries are added by hand: regenerating with swag v1.16.6
also rewrites unrelated definitions on master.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
